From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:39:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] deckcraft-aros: --screenshot draws frames until the picture
 is taken

Problem: --screenshot counts frames before it writes the window's pixels,
  and since the shell has no idle poll an untouched window draws none
  after it settles; the screenshot runs of run k3 waited until input came.
Rationale: while a screenshot is pending the shell asks for a repaint in
  every frame.
Scope: --screenshot only.
Upstream-status: local-only.
Verification: unattended screenshot runs in the port's evidence.
Removal: with the shell.
---
 apps/deckcraft-aros/src/main.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/apps/deckcraft-aros/src/main.rs b/apps/deckcraft-aros/src/main.rs
index 9ebad02491a0fe14f0bb4938c7d5099d543db756..3681a46fcc1bc81570388340029c3c5b1723688c 100644
--- a/apps/deckcraft-aros/src/main.rs
+++ b/apps/deckcraft-aros/src/main.rs
@@ -239,6 +239,11 @@ impl egui_aros::App for Shell {
     }
 
     fn logic(&mut self, ctx: &egui::Context) {
+        // --screenshot counts frames, and with no idle poll an untouched window draws none after
+        // it settles: keep drawing until the picture is taken.
+        if self.screenshot.is_some() && !self.done {
+            ctx.request_repaint();
+        }
         self.app.logic(ctx);
     }
 
